2. NRL Report 7948 letter-to-sound rules
   (ref/NRL-7948-TRANS.SNO, and src/core/bm_rules_en.c generated from it)
================================================================================

    Elovitz, H. S., Johnson, R. W., McHugh, A., & Shore, J. E. (1976).
    "Automatic Translation of English Text to Phonetics by Means of
    Letter-to-Sound Rules." NRL Report 7948, Naval Research Laboratory,
    Washington, D.C. (AD/A021 929)

A work of the United States federal government and therefore in the public
domain. No attribution is legally required. It is given anyway, because these
rules are the reason BENCmouth can read English at all, and because knowing
where they came from is genuinely useful to anyone reading the generated table.

