3. Formant synthesis literature
================================================================================

The synthesizer is an independent implementation from published descriptions —
principally Klatt, D. H. (1980), "Software for a cascade/parallel formant
synthesizer," JASA 67(3), and Klatt & Klatt (1990), JASA 87(2). Those papers are
copyrighted by the Acoustical Society of America and are NOT included in this
repository; only the algorithms they describe are implemented here.

Vowel formant targets derive from the published measurements of Peterson &
Barney (1952).

BENCmouth is not derived from S.A.M. (Software Automatic Mouth) or from any port
or decompilation of it. See ref/README.md for the sources deliberately not
consulted, and why.

