The reserved names restrict *modified* versions from using them, which is why
the file is embedded exactly as released. Do not subset or regenerate it: the
saving is not worth reopening that question.

The OFL permits bundling the font with software provided every copy carries the
copyright notice and the licence "either as stand-alone text files,
human-readable headers or in the appropriate machine-readable metadata fields
